+<p><strong>Chengdu</strong> — Overcast Light & Panda Rules. This guide covers essential filming locations, weather considerations, and permit requirements.</p>
+<div class="takeaways"><h3>⚡ Key Takeaways — Chengdu</h3><ul><li><strong>Top 3 locations:</strong> Chengdu Panda Base, Kuanzhai Alleys, People's Park Teahouses.</li><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Overcast most of the year; humid summers. Best Mar-June and Sept-Nov.</li><li><strong>Airport:</strong> Shuangliu (CTU) 30 min; Tianfu (TFU) 60+ min — check your ticket.</li><li><strong>Permits:</strong> Panda areas strictly regulated; drones banned at the base.</li></ul></div>
+<h2>3 Must-Film Locations in Chengdu</h2>
+<div class="city-card"><h3>1. Chengdu Panda Base</h3><p><strong>Filming tip:</strong> No flash, no tripods; go 8-10 AM when pandas are active; overcast light is soft — expose +0.7.</p></div>
+<div class="city-card"><h3>2. Kuanzhai Alleys</h3><p><strong>Filming tip:</strong> Crowded by 10 AM; shoot at opening; handheld.</p></div>
+<div class="city-card"><h3>3. People's Park Teahouses</h3><p><strong>Filming tip:</strong> Locals are happy to be filmed if you buy a tea and ask first.</p></div>
+<h2>Weather Reality for Videographers</h2><p>Overcast most of the year; humid summers. Best Mar-June and Sept-Nov.</p>
+<div class="tip-box"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Plan shoots according to seasonal conditions. Check forecasts regularly.</div>
+<h2>Airport Transfer</h2><p>Shuangliu (CTU) 30 min; Tianfu (TFU) 60+ min — check your ticket.</p>
+<h2>Permits & Etiquette</h2><p>Panda areas strictly regulated; drones banned at the base.</p>
